// Trader quest chains (pure data). Every trader in Desperanza runs a storyline that sends raiders across
// the three maps: damn_grounds (Dam Grounds), green_gate (Green Gate) and sandy_city (Sandy City).
// `requires` stitches the chains together, so one trader's job often unlocks another's.
//
// Quest: { id, giver, name, desc, requires: [questId...] (ALL must be complete),
//          steps: [...], grants?: { itemId: qty } (handed over on accept), rewards: { xp, coins, items, blueprint? } }
// Step kinds (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) + optional extras:
//   kill    { target: arkId | 'any', count, map?, with?: itemId | [itemIds] | 'grenade' }
//   loot    { item, count, map?, poi? }        pick the item up topside (quest items spawn at `poi`)
//   visit   { map, poi, label?, use?: { itemId: qty } }  reach a POI; `use` = items consumed there
//                                                        (repairs, installs); `label` = UI objective text
//   extract { map? }
//   deliver { item, count }                   hand items in at Desperanza
//   search  { container: kind | [kinds] | 'any', count, map?, poi? }
//           container kinds: src/game/loot.js CONTAINER_LOOT kinds, arc.js ARK_HUSKS ids,
//           plus 'supply_drop' and 'bee_hive'.
// POI ids used here are listed (with display names) in QUEST_POIS at the bottom.
// The HUD shortens a visit label to its first word + the POI name, so labels start with a verb.

